WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:06.520
Are you left-handed?

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.280
If so, one in ten people
around the world is like you.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:13.280
However, nine out of ten people
are right-handed.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:22.040
Stone tools suggest that most of our
ancestors were, like most of us,

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:23.080
right-handed.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.960
It's hard to pin down when
left-handedness started,

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.200
but we do have evidence that there
were left-handed Neanderthals

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.760
500,000 years ago.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.040
How do we know this?

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:36.560
Well, they were probably eating raw
meat, which is tough old stuff.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.800
Archaeologists think the Neanderthals
would sink their teeth in,

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:43.480
and then use a sharp piece of stone
to cut the meat near their mouth.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.720
Sometimes the stone slipped.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.160
And from the direction
of the scratches,

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:52.880
10% of Neanderthals seem to have
held the cutter in their left hand.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.960
For right-handers, it's normally
the left side of the brain

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:03.120
that's associated
with speech and language.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:04.880
What though if you are left-handed?

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.600
Despite using their left hand
for writing,

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:11.720
two thirds of left-handers
are just like right-handers,

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.120
in having language
in their left brain.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.200
But, a third of left-handers

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.080
have language in the
right side of their brain -

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:21.440
the opposite of right-handers.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.720
Left-handers are much more variable

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:25.800
in the ways their brains
are organised.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:28.920
In contrast, right-hander's brains
are off-the-peg.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.720
Left-handedness is therefore
much more of a mixture

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:34.240
of strengths and weaknesses,
pros and cons

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:37.560
coming from having a somewhat
differently organised brain.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.040
Is your baby sucking its thumb?

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.200
Psychologist Peter Hepper in Belfast

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.680
studied several hundred scans

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:50.960
where the baby in the womb
was seen sucking its thumb.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:55.000
About 90% of babies sucked
their right thumb.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:57.000
And at twelve years old,

00:01:57.080 --> 00:02:00.760
almost all of those right thumb
suckers were right-handed.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.160
Whereas three-quarters
of the left thumb suckers

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:05.720
would become left-handed.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.480
Genes are clearly also important.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:09.680
One left-handed parent,

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:11.720
and you're more likely
to be left-handed yourself.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:15.120
Both parents left-handed,
and you're even more likely.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.880
About a one in four chance.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:20.400
Infants often go through
a random chaotic phase

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:23.320
where they use the right hand
one day, and the left the other,

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:24.880
perplexing their parents.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:28.880
By about two-years-old, their
handedness is usually consistent.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.160
If you practise long and hard enough,

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:39.080
then you can probably do anything
equally well with either hand.

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:43.760
Concert pianists are a good example,
though it does take dedication.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:47.880
In 1797, the right-handed Admiral
Lord Nelson,

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:50.720
had his right elbow
shattered by a musket ball.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.360
The arm was amputated.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:53.920
Within six months though,

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.800
Nelson had learnt to write
fluently with his left hand.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.160
But the motivation was
there, of course.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:02.760
Professional sports players are
also motivated to practise,

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:05.080
as it can give an added
edge in competiton.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:08.480
Footballers train to kick well
with either foot,

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:11.920
and when practising they use
both feet confidently and well.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.600
But under pressure,
when the action's hot,

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:17.480
they often revert to using
their dominant foot.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:21.480
Even if it means taking an extra
half-step before shooting for goal.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:24.600
Reversing your natural sidedness
does come with a cost.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:28.280
You could be almost equally good
with each hand or foot,

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:31.440
but the price would be
so much time practising,

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:33.840
that you probably wouldn't
do anything else with your life.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:43.000
The list of famous left-handers
seems pretty impressive.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:49.200
Albert Einstein, Beethoven,
Bob Dylan, Picasso, Neil Armstrong,

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:53.240
Winston Churchill, Benjamin Franklin,
Marilyn Monroe,

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:57.080
all are claimed, on the internet,
to be left-handed.

00:03:57.160 --> 00:04:00.400
And in each case,
it's almost certainly wrong.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:05.160
The evidence of left-handedness
is often very dodgy indeed.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:06.200
For instance,

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:09.320
there's a book with a painting of
Beethoven writing with his left hand,

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.120
the picture has clearly been flipped.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:14.760
There are many reasons why
people may wrongly claim

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:17.160
that famous individuals
are left-handed.

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:20.600
Tribal loyalty
and the reflected glory

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:23.840
of feeling part of the same
handedness club are just two of them.

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:26.160
Perhaps when it comes down to it,

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:29.880
there is a little bit of the
left-hander in each of us.

